# ========================================================
# Smart Resume AI Builder — Environment Variables Example
# ========================================================
# HOW TO SET UP LOCALLY:
# 1. Copy this file to a new file named .env in the project root or backend directory:
#      copy .env.example .env     (Windows CMD)
#      cp .env.example .env       (macOS / Linux / PowerShell)
# 2. Get a free Groq API key from https://console.groq.com/keys
# 3. Replace 'your_groq_api_key_here' below with your actual key (starts with gsk_...)
# 4. Start the backend:
#      python app.py
# 5. The application securely accesses Groq exclusively through backend API routes.
#    NEVER commit your .env file or real API keys to version control.
# ========================================================

# Flask Server Port (Default: 5000)
PORT=5000

# Groq Cloud AI Engine (Required for Llama 3.3 70B generation)
# Obtain a free API key from https://console.groq.com/keys
GROQ_API_KEY=your_groq_api_key_here

# Optional: Google Gemini AI Fallback
# Obtain an API key from https://aistudio.google.com/
GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here

# ========================================================
# SMTP Email Service Configuration
# Authoritative server-side dispatch of 6-digit verification codes.
# ========================================================
# HOW TO CONFIGURE GMAIL SMTP:
# 1. SMTP_HOST: Set to smtp.gmail.com
# 2. SMTP_PORT: Set to 587 (TLS / STARTTLS encryption)
# 3. Security Requirements for Google Accounts:
#    - You MUST enable "2-Step Verification" on your Google Account:
#      Go to https://myaccount.google.com/security -> 2-Step Verification
#    - You MUST generate a 16-character "Google App Password":
#      Go to https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords
#      Select app name "Smart Resume AI" and click Generate.
#      (Standard Google account passwords CANNOT be used over SMTP and will be rejected with code 535)
# 4. SMTP_USER: Your full Gmail address (e.g. sender@gmail.com)
# 5. SMTP_PASSWORD: The generated 16-character App Password (spaces are automatically removed by backend)
# 6. SMTP_FROM: Must match your Gmail address or authorized sending alias
# 7. SMTP_USE_TLS: Set to true for port 587
#
# CRITICAL: Keep your real credentials in .env only; NEVER commit .env to version control.
# ========================================================
SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
SMTP_PORT=587
SMTP_USER=your_email@gmail.com
SMTP_PASSWORD=your_app_password_here
SMTP_FROM=your_email@gmail.com
SMTP_USE_TLS=true

